    "body": "The duplicate wedge in #795: a copy of the Brick and everything under it, placed beside the original as its own Tower.\n\nObjectives:\n- [ ] Export one node's sub-tree as an `ExportedProject`, reusing the workspace exporter's node writer.\n- [ ] Build the copy with `resolveIds` on `remint` and `reconstructTowers`, so it carries fresh ids; `validateProject` is for payloads from outside the app.\n- [ ] Copy the same reach a drag carries: the Brick, its arguments, its cavity contents and its `next` chain.\n- [ ] Place it as a new Tower offset from the original and connected to nothing, then run its layout and sync both Collision spaces.\n- [ ] Preserve fold states through the copy, the Brick's own and any nested inside it.\n- [ ] Cover it with tests: the shape of the copy, its ids being fresh, the fold states, and the original left untouched.\n",
